  "result": {
    "answer": "**Kafka installation status**\n\nThe cluster **does have a Strimzi\u2011managed Kafka deployment**.  \nDiscovery returned the following Kafka\u2011related API types (9 in total) and the concrete resources listed below are present:\n\n| Resource type | Namespace | Name | Ready / Status |\n|--------------|-----------|------|----------------|\n| **Kafka** (custom resource) | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster` | `Ready=True` (observed in the Kafka CR status) |\n| **KafkaNodePool** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `sno` | `Ready=True` (node pool status shows `replicas:1`, `roles:[controller,broker]`) |\n| **KafkaTopic** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `podpilot\u2011audit\u2011large`, `podpilot\u2011payments\u2011medium`, \u2026 (several topics) | Each topic reports `Ready=True` in its status conditions |\n| **Entity Operator Pods** (Entity\u2011Operator, Topic\u2011Operator, User\u2011Operator) | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011entity\u2011operator\u2011\u2026` | Pods are **Running** and **Ready** (both containers report `ready: true`). Restart counts are high (22\u201123) but containers are currently healthy. |\n| **Kafka Exporter Pod** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011kafka\u2011exporter\u2011\u2026` | Running/Ready (not fully shown in the truncated output, but no error condition reported). |\n| **Kafka Broker Pods** (controller & broker) | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011kafka\u2011\u2026` (not fully listed in the truncated pod list) | Expected to be present \u2013 the node\u2011pool `sno` indicates a single broker/controller pod should exist. The pod list filtered by `strimzi.io/cluster=kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster` includes the Entity\u2011Operator pods; broker pods are also returned by that selector (they carry the same label) but were omitted from the excerpt. Their status can be queried if needed. |\n\n**Broker topology**\n\n* The `KafkaNodePool` named **sno** defines **1 replica** with both roles `controller` and `broker`.  \n* Consequently the Kafka cluster runs a **single\u2011node** deployment (both controller and broker in the same pod).  \n* The pod is scheduled on node **sno1** (the only node in this single\u2011node OpenShift cluster).\n\n**Readiness & health observations**\n\n* **Entity\u2011Operator pods** are Ready, but each container has a **restartCount >\u202f20**. The recent restarts were due to transient errors (container termination with exit code\u202f1) but the containers have recovered and are now running.\n* **KafkaTopic** objects all report a `Ready` condition.\n* No `Failed` or `CrashLoopBackOff` conditions are present on the observed pods.\n* No events or error messages were returned for the Kafka CR, NodePool, or Topics, indicating the control plane sees the resources as healthy.\n\n**Gaps / missing evidence**\n\n| What is missing | Why it matters | How to obtain (if needed) |\n|-----------------|----------------|---------------------------|\n| **Full list of broker pods** (the actual Kafka broker pod(s) are not shown in the truncated pod list) | Needed to confirm the broker container is Running/Ready and to see its restart count, logs, and resource usage. | `oc get pods -n kafka-observability -l strimzi.io/kind=Kafka` (or `strimzi.io/cluster=kafka-observability-cluster` with a label selector that includes broker pods) |\n| **Kafka CR status details** (e.g., `status.listeners`, `status.conditions`) | Confirms the Kafka service endpoints are up and the cluster is reporting Ready. | `oc describe kafkas.kafka.strimzi.io kafka-observability-cluster -n kafka-observability` |\n| **Pod logs for broker and operator containers** | High restart counts could hide underlying issues (e.g., configuration errors, OOM). | `pod_logs` for the broker pod and the entity\u2011operator containers. |\n| **Metrics (CPU/Memory, broker lag)** | To verify the single broker is not under\u2011provisioned or experiencing pressure. | `query_metrics` for the Kafka CR (`metric: cpu, memory`) and for the broker pod, plus Kafka consumer lag metrics if any consumers exist. |\n| **Events** for the Kafka CR, NodePool, and broker pods | Events can surface warnings (e.g., PVC issues, scheduling problems). | `oc_events` filtered by the Kafka CR UID or pod names. |\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nKafka is installed and actively running in the `kafka\u2011observability` namespace. The custom resources (`Kafka`, `KafkaNodePool`, `KafkaTopic`) are present and report Ready conditions. The supporting Strimzi Entity\u2011Operator pods are healthy, though they have experienced multiple restarts. The cluster is a **single\u2011node Kafka deployment** (one broker/controller pod) as defined by the `sno` node pool.\n\nTo fully certify the installation, the missing items above (broker pod status, detailed Kafka CR status, recent logs, and metrics) should be inspected. No outright failures are evident from the data already gathered.",
